{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/122777-strength-successes-to-break-bullet-resistant-glass","id":122777,"title":"Strength/successes to break bullet-resistant glass?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-30T16:58:07-07:00","id":122777,"title":"Strength/successes to break bullet-resistant glass?","content":"Let's say you're trying to punch through a car window that's made from bullet-resistant glass. How many cumulative successes on a Strength+Athletics or Strength+Brawl (not which one is best) do you think would be required to inside the car?<br /> <br /> What about ripping open/off the door of a car that's been reinforced with discreet armor plating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T20:40:48-07:00","id":122904,"title":"","content":"It depends a bit on the specific type of material used and how the window is secured. If the window can roll down or not matters significantly to how easy it would be to remove.<br /> <br /> AFAIK most armored cars don't reinforce the hinges on the doors against being ripped off though. It would be a bit tougher because the hinges are tougher to account for the increased weight, but I'm not sure enough to really make a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T22:27:32-07:00","id":122975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/122777-strength-successes-to-break-bullet-resistant-glass?p=122904#post122904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK most armored cars don't reinforce the hinges on the doors against being ripped off though. It would be a bit tougher because the hinges are tougher to account for the increased weight, but I'm not sure enough to really make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>This car is more likely than most to be hardened against some Lasombra trying to rip the doors off, but point taken. Let's assume the window doesn't roll down.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T00:16:36-07:00","id":123002,"title":"","content":"Then... punching through is going to be problematic. The amount of force you're talking about is high enough that without supernatural powers (aka lots of Fortitude and high Stamina) it is more likely that they're hand would being turned into a bloody stump than break an acrylic or polycarbonate Level 3+ rated surface that's completely secured to the frame of the door.<br /> <br /> To give you an idea, hand gun bullets that strike high end acrylic armor tend to <i>melt</i> and splatter on impact. They are stopped so completely that all the force of the impact turns into heat that melts the bullet almost instantly.<br /> <br /> The key to forcing through those materials is generally repeat pinpoint impacts on the same spot because once you compromise their structural integrity, even in a relatively small area, it drastically decreases the effectiveness of the whole plane. Or heat because they will melt and deform if exposed to enough of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T01:07:36-07:00","id":123014,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that gives me a very good idea of how to run a material like that.<br /> <br /> So, I'd imagine that if the windows still could roll down the weak point becomes the mechanism. Bash the window enough and you can dislodge it within the door, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T08:44:20-07:00","id":123189,"title":"","content":"Damaging objects is a guaranteed full success attack roll and you roll the successes for strength directly if I well remember so that would be brawl. The strength table is pretty descriptive of the amount of strength a individual has, at 6 the kindred's throwing bikes and flipping cars at 7 and 5 says they can bash down a metal fire door. I think I'd require between 6 to break down the glass and then give it an appropriately large health pool and no soak and maybe reflecting the damage back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>former lightmaguz","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/514-auron","name":"Auron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T11:43:32-07:00","id":123316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/122777-strength-successes-to-break-bullet-resistant-glass?p=123014#post123014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'd imagine that if the windows still could roll down the weak point becomes the mechanism. Bash the window enough and you can dislodge it within the door, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that part of the reason these materials work so well is that they're plastics. They can flex. If they can roll down, a high Potence vampire could probably flex the top of the window enough to push down into the mechanism holding the window up until it breaks and the window slides down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}